{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AiXuAFmXNYkVjAPVwzfSH2","type":"tool_result","content":"## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, num\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\n\n## 21d. Shell\n\n- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\n- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\n- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\n- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\n- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\n- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\n- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\n- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\n- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\n- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over t\n- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\n- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\n- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\n\n## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eff3345-97e6-4e65-b411-5b68a8aed193","uuid":"4aae3ebc-0fff-4702-aaf7-7f0e65656312","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:55:42.611Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and i